-- title:
--   One-step lift of an invariant element modulo I^{N+1}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a commutative ring $B$, and let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$ in the sense of the project: a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F$ over $B$ together with an action of $\mathbb Z_p^2$ by endomorphism series and a series $\varpi$, all law endomorphisms of $F$, subject to $\mathrm{act}(1)=\mathrm{id}$, multiplicativity and additivity of $\mathrm{act}$, $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(a)=\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{Frob}\,a)\circ\varpi$; only $F$ enters the statement. Let $I\subseteq B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ be an ideal such that some power $X_i^q$ lies in $I$ for both variables, and such that for $f\in I$ the series $f(F_1,F_2)$ lies in the ideal generated by the images of $I$ under the two coordinate inclusions $B[\![x]\!]\to B[\![x',x'']\!]$. Let $L$ be a commutative $B$-Hopf algebra, free and finite as a $B$-module, and $\pi : B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]\to L$ a surjective $B$-algebra map with kernel $I$ such that each $\pi(X_i)$ is nilpotent, $\pi$ is evaluation of power series at the points $\pi(X_i)$, the comultiplication of $\pi(X_i)$ is the value of $F_i$ at the points $\pi(X_j)\otimes 1$ and $1\otimes\pi(X_j)$, and the counit of $\pi(G)$ is the constant coefficient of $G$. Let $N\neq 0$, and let $\delta$ and $\delta'$ be $B$-algebra maps from $B[\![x]\!]/I^N$, respectively $B[\![x]\!]/I^{N+1}$, to their tensor products with $L$ over $B$, each given on the class of $G$ by evaluating $G$ at the points obtained by evaluating $F_i$ at $\overline{X_j}\otimes 1$ and $1\otimes\pi(X_j)$. Then for every $f\in I$ whose class modulo $I^N$ is invariant, i.e. $\delta(\bar f)=\bar f\otimes 1$, there exists $s\in I^N$ with $\delta'(\overline{f-s})=\overline{f-s}\otimes 1$.
--
--   This is the inductive step of the lifting argument which shows that the ideal cutting out a finite free infinitesimal subgroup of the formal $\mathcal O_D$-module is generated by elements invariant under the coaction: the obstruction to invariance one level further is a Hopf-module cocycle on $I^N/I^{N+1}$ and is therefore a coboundary. It is cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.eq_span_setOf_invariant_of_subgroup_ideal_of_free`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.eq_span_setOf_invariant_of_subgroup_ideal_of_free), and in turn uses the existence of the level coactions together with the cocycle-splitting lemma [`HopfAlgebra.exists_eq_coaction_sub_tmul_one_of_cocycle`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_eq_coaction_sub_tmul_one_of_cocycle).
